  evidenceNote:
    "Accessibility is a normative concept, not an experimental effect. It rests on normative instruments (the CRPD, whose authority comes from adoption by states, and consensus standards such as WCAG), on conceptual frameworks from disabled people's movements and disability studies (the social model) and from WHO (the ICF), on official reports that synthesise evidence about barriers, prevalence and inequities (WHO 2011 and 2022), and on professional practice. Replication does not apply to treaties, standards or definitions; prevalence figures are report estimates; and evidence that a particular product is accessible comes from evaluation with assistive technologies and disabled people, not from conformance alone.",

